[Event "01. The final picture (1/8)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "1k6/4R3/8/8/8/8/8/K2R4 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "01. The final picture (1/8)"]
[LineDescription "The ladder's last rung: one rook on the 7th rank, the other checks on the 8th."]

{[%csl Bc8,Ba8] Welcome to the ladder mate! Two heavy pieces (two rooks, or a
queen and a rook) can mate the lone king without any help from your own king.
First the goal: what the mate looks like on the edge of the board. Mate in 1
with two rooks: one rook holds the 7th rank, so the other only has to check
along the 8th. Blue: the squares the black king can step to. Find the check that
takes them all away.} 1. Rd8# {[%csl Rb8] Checkmate! The rook on d8 checks along
the 8th rank and the rook on e7 holds the 7th: the king has no square left.} *

