b7 stands right next to the king, protected by the rook on d7: the king can
neither take it nor run.} *

[Event "02. The ladder with two rooks (1/12)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "8/1R6/8/5k2/3R4/8/8/1K6 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "02. The ladder with two rooks (1/12)"]
[LineDescription "The ladder: one rook holds the wall, the other checks one row further; repeat up to the edge."]

{[%csl Be5,Bf5,Bg5,Bh5,Be6,Bf6,Bg6,Bh6] The ladder (also called the lawnmower):
one rook holds a row, the "wall", so the king cannot go back; the other rook
gives check one row further, so the king has to climb. Then the rooks swap
roles, row by row, until the king is mated on the edge. Your king stays at home.
Climb the ladder: check, then let the other rook take the next row, and so on up
to the 8th rank. Blue: the box, every square the black king can still reach.
Watch it shrink row by row.} 1. Rb5+ {Check on the 5th rank! The rook on d4
holds the 4th rank, so the king has to climb to the 6th.} 1... Ke6 {[%csl
Be6,Bf6,Bg6,Bh6,Be7,Bf7,Bg7,Bh7,Be8,Bf8,Bg8,Bh8]} 2. Rh4 {A quiet move: the rook
slides along the 4th rank to the far side (h4), so that the king cannot attack
it when it gives the next check.} 2... Kd6 {[%csl
Bc6,Bd6,Be6,Bf6,Bg6,Bc7,Bd7,Be7,Bf7,Bg7,Bc8,Bd8,Be8,Bf8,Bg8]} 3. Rh6+ {Check on
the 6th rank: up to the 7th.} 3... Kc7 {[%csl
Bc7,Bd7,Be7,Bf7,Bg7,Bc8,Bd8,Be8,Bf8,Bg8]} 4. Rg5 {The rook slides to the far
side again (g5) before the next check.} 4... Kb7 {[%csl
Ba7,Bb7,Bc7,Bd7,Be7,Bf7,Ba8,Bb8,Bc8,Bd8,Be8,Bf8]} 5. Rg7+ {Check on the 7th
rank: up to the 8th.} 5... Ka8 {[%csl Ba8,Bb8,Bc8,Bd8,Be8,Bf8]} 6. Rh8# {[%csl
Ra8] Checkmate! The rook on h8 checks along the 8th rank and the rook on g7
holds the 7th: the king has no square left.} *

[Event "02. The ladder with two rooks (2/12)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "8/8/8/8/5k2/7R/KR6/8 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "02. The ladder with two rooks (2/12)"]
[LineDescription "The ladder: one rook holds the wall, the other checks one row further; repeat up to the edge."]

{[%csl
Bc4,Bd4,Be4,Bf4,Bg4,Bc5,Bd5,Be5,Bf5,Bg5,Bc6,Bd6,Be6,Bf6,Bg6,Bc7,Bd7,Be7,Bf7,Bg7,Bc8,Bd8,Be8,Bf8,Bg8]
Another ladder: wall, check, wall, check, up to the edge.} 1. Rb4+ {Check on the
4th rank! The rook on h3 holds the 3rd rank, so the king has to climb to the
5th.} 1... Ke5 {[%csl
Bc5,Bd5,Be5,Bf5,Bg5,Bc6,Bd6,Be6,Bf6,Bg6,Bc7,Bd7,Be7,Bf7,Bg7,Bc8,Bd8,Be8,Bf8,Bg8]}
2. Rh5+ {Check on the 5th rank: up to the 6th.} 2... Kd6 {[%csl
Bc6,Bd6,Be6,Bf6,Bg6,Bc7,Bd7,Be7,Bf7,Bg7,Bc8,Bd8,Be8,Bf8,Bg8]} 3. Rb6+ {Check on
the 6th rank: up to the 7th.} 3... Kc7 {[%csl
Bc7,Bd7,Be7,Bf7,Bg7,Bc8,Bd8,Be8,Bf8,Bg8] The king attacks the rook on b6!} 4.
Rg6 {The king attacked the rook: it moves to the far side, g6, out of the king's
reach and still holds the 6th rank.} 4... Kb7 {[%csl
Ba7,Bb7,Bc7,Bd7,Be7,Bf7,Ba8,Bb8,Bc8,Bd8,Be8,Bf8]} 5. Rh7+ {Check on the 7th
rank: up to the 8th.} 5... Ka8 {[%csl Ba8,Bb8,Bc8,Bd8,Be8,Bf8]} 6. Rg8# {[%csl
Ra8] Checkmate! The rook on g8 checks along the 8th rank and the rook on h7
holds the 7th: the king has no square left.} *

[Event "02. The ladder with two rooks (3/12)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "1R6/8/8/2k5/6R1/8/K7/8 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "02. The ladder with two rooks (3/12)"]
[LineDescription "The ladder: one rook holds the wall, the other checks one row further; repeat up to the edge."]

{[%csl Bc5,Bd5,Be5,Bf5,Bc6,Bd6,Be6,Bf6,Bc7,Bd7,Be7,Bf7] Which rook holds the
wall, and which one checks next?} 1. Rd8 {The rook cuts the king off along the
d-file: the box shrinks to 9 squares.} 1... Kc6 {[%csl
Ba5,Bb5,Bc5,Ba6,Bb6,Bc6,Ba7,Bb7,Bc7]} 2. Rg6+ {Check! The king's toughest reply
is to step up to c7, where it is locked in the top 2 rows.} 2... Kc7 {[%csl
Ba7,Bb7,Bc7] The king attacks the rook on d8!} 3. Rh8 {The king attacked the
rook: it moves to the far side, h8, out of the king's reach and still holds the
8th rank.} 3... Kb7 {[%csl Ba7,Bb7,Bc7,Bd7,Be7,Bf7]} 4. Rh7+ {Check on the 7th
rank! The rook on g6 holds the 6th rank, so the king has to climb to the 8th.}
4... Ka8 {[%csl Ba8,Bb8,Bc8,Bd8,Be8,Bf8]} 5. Rg8# {[%csl Ra8] Checkmate! The
rook on g8 checks along the 8th rank and the rook on h7 holds the 7th: the king
has no square left.} *

