[LineName "02. The ladder with two rooks (11/12)"]
[LineDescription "The ladder: one rook holds the wall, the other checks one row further; repeat up to the edge."]

{[%csl
Bb3,Bc3,Bd3,Be3,Bf3,Bg3,Bh3,Bb4,Bc4,Bd4,Be4,Bf4,Bg4,Bh4,Bb5,Bc5,Bd5,Be5,Bf5,Bg5,Bh5,Bb6,Bc6,Bd6,Be6,Bf6,Bg6,Bh6,Bb7,Bc7,Bd7,Be7,Bf7,Bg7,Bh7]
Which rook holds the wall, and which one checks next?} 1. R2a6 {The rook takes
the 6th rank: the wall moves up, and the king is locked in the top 2 rows.} 1...
Kd7 {[%csl Bb7,Bc7,Bd7,Be7,Bf7,Bg7,Bh7]} 2. R8a7+ {Check on the 7th rank! The
rook on a6 holds the 6th rank, so the king has to climb to the 8th.} 2... Kc8
{[%csl Bb8,Bc8,Bd8,Be8,Bf8,Bg8,Bh8]} 3. Rb6 {A quiet move: the rook goes to b6,
ready to mate while the other rook keeps the king in.} 3... Kd8 {[%csl
Bc8,Bd8,Be8,Bf8,Bg8,Bh8]} 4. Rb8# {[%csl Rd8] Checkmate! The rook on b8 checks
along the 8th rank and the rook on a7 holds the 7th: the king has no square
left.} *

