[LineName "02. The ladder with two rooks (12/12)"]
[LineDescription "The ladder: one rook holds the wall, the other checks one row further; repeat up to the edge."]

{[%csl
Bc2,Bd2,Be2,Bf2,Bg2,Bh2,Bc3,Bd3,Be3,Bf3,Bg3,Bh3,Bc4,Bd4,Be4,Bf4,Bg4,Bh4,Bc5,Bd5,Be5,Bf5,Bg5,Bh5,Bc6,Bd6,Be6,Bf6,Bg6,Bh6,Bc7,Bd7,Be7,Bf7,Bg7,Bh7]
Push the king up row by row. Keep both rooks out of its reach.} 1. R1b6 {The
rook takes the 6th rank: the wall moves up, and the king is locked in the top 2
rows.} 1... Ke7 {[%csl Bc7,Bd7,Be7,Bf7,Bg7,Bh7]} 2. R8b7+ {Check on the 7th
rank! The rook on b6 holds the 6th rank, so the king has to climb to the 8th.}
2... Kd8 {[%csl Bc8,Bd8,Be8,Bf8,Bg8,Bh8]} 3. Rc6 {A quiet move: the rook goes to
c6, ready to mate while the other rook keeps the king in.} 3... Ke8 {[%csl
Bd8,Be8,Bf8,Bg8,Bh8]} 4. Rc8# {[%csl Re8] Checkmate! The rook on c8 checks along
the 8th rank and the rook on b7 holds the 7th: the king has no square left.} *

[Event "03. The king attacks a rook: switch sides (1/8)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "8/8/1k6/R7/8/8/8/K5R1 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "03. The king attacks a rook: switch sides (1/8)"]
[LineDescription "An attacked rook goes to the far side along its row: the wall stays and the king cannot reach it."]

{[%csl Bb6,Bc6,Bd6,Be6,Bf6,Bb7,Bc7,Bd7,Be7,Bf7,Bb8,Bc8,Bd8,Be8,Bf8] The black
king will try to catch a rook that stands near it. Don't defend the rook and
don't give up the row: move it along the same row to the far side of the board,
out of the king's reach. The wall stays, and the ladder goes on. The black king
is next to one of your rooks. Move that rook along its row to the far side of
the board. Blue: the box, every square the black king can still reach.} 1. Rh5
{The king attacked the rook: it moves to the far side, h5, out of the king's
reach and still holds the 5th rank.} 1... Kc6 {[%csl
Ba6,Bb6,Bc6,Bd6,Be6,Bf6,Ba7,Bb7,Bc7,Bd7,Be7,Bf7,Ba8,Bb8,Bc8,Bd8,Be8,Bf8]} 2.
Rg6+ {Check on the 6th rank! The rook on h5 holds the 5th rank, so the king has
to climb to the 7th.} 2... Kb7 {[%csl
Ba7,Bb7,Bc7,Bd7,Be7,Bf7,Ba8,Bb8,Bc8,Bd8,Be8,Bf8]} 3. Rh7+ {Check on the 7th
rank: up to the 8th.} 3... Ka8 {[%csl Ba8,Bb8,Bc8,Bd8,Be8,Bf8]} 4. Rg8# {[%csl
Ra8] Checkmate! The rook on g8 checks along the 8th rank and the rook on h7
holds the 7th: the king has no square left.} *

