[LineDescription "Queen and rook climb the ladder like two rooks, only faster."]

{[%csl Bc5,Bd5,Be5,Bf5,Bg5,Bb6,Bd6,Be6,Bf6,Bg6] Queen and rook climb the same
ladder, only faster: the queen covers rows, columns and diagonals at once. One
piece holds the wall, the other checks one row further, until the king is mated
on the edge. Climb the ladder with queen and rook: one piece holds the wall, the
other checks one row further. Blue: the box, every square the black king can
still reach.} 1. Rh5+ {Check on the 5th rank! The queen on a4 holds the 4th
rank, so the king has to climb to the 6th.} 1... Kd6 {[%csl
Bb6,Bd6,Be6,Bf6,Bg6,Bb7,Bc7,Be7,Bf7,Bg7,Bb8,Bc8,Bd8,Bf8,Bg8]} 2. Qa6+ {Check on
the 6th rank: up to the 7th.} 2... Kc7 {[%csl
Bc7,Bd7,Be7,Bf7,Bg7,Bb8,Bd8,Be8,Bf8,Bg8]} 3. Rh7+ {Check on the 7th rank: up to
the 8th.} 3... Kb8 {[%csl Bb8]} 4. Qb7# {[%csl Rb8] Checkmate! The queen on b7
stands right next to the king, protected by the rook on h7: the king can neither
take it nor run.} *

