[LineName "04. The ladder with queen and rook (9/10)"]
[LineDescription "Queen and rook climb the ladder like two rooks, only faster."]

{[%csl
Ba4,Bb4,Bc4,Bd4,Be4,Ba5,Bb5,Bc5,Bd5,Bf5,Ba6,Bb6,Bc6,Be6,Bf6,Ba7,Bb7,Bd7,Be7,Bf7]
Queen and rook: which piece holds the wall, which one checks?} 1. Qe5 {The queen
takes the 5th rank: the wall moves up, and the king is locked in the top 3
rows.} 1... Kb6 {[%csl Ba6,Bb6,Bc6,Ba7,Bb7,Bd7]} 2. Rg6+ {Check on the 6th rank!
The queen on e5 holds the 5th rank, so the king has to climb to the 7th.} 2...
Kb7 {[%csl Ba7,Bb7,Bd7,Ba8,Bc8,Bd8]} 3. Qe7+ {Check on the 7th rank: up to the
8th.} 3... Ka8 {[%csl Ba8,Bb8,Bc8]} 4. Rg8# {[%csl Ra8] Checkmate! The rook on
g8 checks along the 8th rank and the queen on e7 holds the 7th: the king has no
square left.} *

