edge with queen and rook, row by row.} 1. Qf5 {The queen takes the 5th rank: the
wall moves up, and the king is locked in the top 3 rows.} 1... Kd6 {[%csl
Ba6,Bb6,Bc6,Bd6] The king attacks the rook on e7!} 2. Re6+ {Check on the 6th
rank! The queen on f5 holds the 5th rank, so the king has to climb to the 7th.}
2... Kc7 {[%csl Ba7,Bb7,Bc7,Bd7,Ba8,Bb8,Bc8,Bd8]} 3. Qf7+ {Check on the 7th
rank: up to the 8th.} 3... Kb8 {[%csl Ba8,Bb8,Bc8,Bd8]} 4. Re8# {[%csl Rb8]
Checkmate! The rook on e8 checks along the 8th rank and the queen on f7 holds
the 7th: the king has no square left.} *

[Event "05. Don't stalemate! (1/8)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "2k5/8/KR6/3R4/8/8/8/8 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "05. Don't stalemate! (1/8)"]
[LineDescription "Before a quiet move with two rooks, check that the king still has a square."]

{[%csl Bc7] [%cal Rb6b7] With two heavy pieces it is easy to take every square
from the king without giving check: that is stalemate, and the game is a draw.
Before each quiet move, make sure the king still has a square, or that your move
gives check. Two rooks near the king in the corner: one careless quiet move and
it is stalemate. Blue: the squares the black king can step to. Red arrow: a
natural move that would be stalemate.} 1. Rc6+ {Not Rb7: that takes the king's
last square without check, and it is stalemate! Check! The king has only one
square left: b8.} 1... Kb8 {[%csl Ba8]} 2. Rd8# {Checkmate! The rook on d8
checks along the 8th rank, and the rook on c6 covers the squares in front of the
king.} *

[Event "05. Don't stalemate! (2/8)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "k2K4/2R5/3R4/8/8/8/8/8 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "05. Don't stalemate! (2/8)"]
[LineDescription "Before a quiet move with two rooks, check that the king still has a square."]

{[%csl Bb8] [%cal Rd8c8,Rd6b6] Two rooks again: check, or leave the king a
square.} 1. Rdd7 {Not Kc8 or Rb6: each of them takes the king's last square
without check, and it is stalemate! A waiting move: the rook goes to d7. The box
stays closed, and now Black has to move.} 1... Kb8 {[%csl Ba8] [%cal Rc7a7]
Careful: Ra7 would be stalemate.} 2. Rc8# {Checkmate! The rook on c8 checks
along the 8th rank and the rook on d7 holds the 7th: the king has no square
left.} *

[Event "05. Don't stalemate! (3/8)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "1k1K4/3R4/3R4/8/8/8/8/8 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "05. Don't stalemate! (3/8)"]
[LineDescription "Before a quiet move with two rooks, check that the king still has a square."]

{[%csl Ba8] [%cal Rd6a6] Two rooks again: check, or leave the king a square.} 1.
Rc6 {Not Ra6: that takes the king's last square without check, and it is
stalemate! A quiet move: the rook goes to c6, ready to mate while the other rook
keeps the king in.} 1... Ka8 {[%csl Bb8] [%cal Rd8c8,Rc6b6] Careful: Kc8 or Rb6
would be stalemate.} 2. Rc8# {Checkmate! The rook on c8 checks along the 8th
rank and the rook on d7 holds the 7th: the king has no square left.} *

[Event "05. Don't stalemate! (4/8)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "3k4/8/1KR5/4R3/8/8/8/8 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "05. Don't stalemate! (4/8)"]
[LineDescription "Before a quiet move with two rooks, check that the king still has a square."]

{[%csl Bd7] [%cal Rc6c7] Two rooks again: check, or leave the king a square.} 1.
Rd6+ {Not Rc7: that takes the king's last square without check, and it is
stalemate! Check! The king has only one square left: c8.} 1... Kc8 {[%csl Bb8]}
2. Re8# {Checkmate! The rook on e8 checks along the 8th rank, and the rook on d6
covers the squares in front of the king.} *

[Event "05. Don't stalemate! (5/8)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "3R4/k7/8/7Q/8/8/8/K7 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "05. Don't stalemate! (5/8)"]
[LineDescription "The queen is the piece that stalemates most easily: count the king's squares first."]

{[%csl Bb7,Bb6,Ba6] [%cal Rh5b5] The queen takes so many squares that a quiet
queen move easily stalemates.} 1. Qg6 {Not Qb5: that takes all 3 of the king's
squares without check, and it is stalemate! The queen takes the 6th rank: the
wall moves up, and the king is locked in the top 2 rows.} 1... Kb7 {[%csl
Bc7,Ba7]} 2. Rd7+ {Check on the 7th rank! The queen on g6 holds the 6th rank, so
the king has to climb to the 8th.} 2... Kc8 {[%csl Bd7,Bb8] [%cal Rg6d6] The
king attacks the rook on d7! Careful: Qd6 would be stalemate.} 3. Qe8#
{Checkmate! The queen on e8 checks along the 8th rank and the rook on d7 holds
the 7th: the king has no square left.} *

[Event "05. Don't stalemate! (6/8)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "2k5/8/8/8/8/8/4Q3/KR6 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "05. Don't stalemate! (6/8)"]
[LineDescription "The queen is the piece that stalemates most easily: count the king's squares first."]

{[%csl Bd8,Bd7,Bc7] [%cal Re2e7] Queen and rook again: careful with quiet queen
moves.} 1. Qa6+ {Not Qe7: that takes all 3 of the king's squares without check,
and it is stalemate! Check! The king has to step away; its toughest reply is
c7.} 1... Kc7 {[%csl Bd8,Bd7]} 2. Rb7+ {Check on the 7th rank! The queen on a6
holds the 6th rank, so the king has to climb to the 8th.} 2... Kc8 {[%csl Bd8]
[%cal Ra6b6] Careful: Qb6 would be stalemate.} 3. Qa8# {Checkmate! The queen on
a8 checks along the 8th rank and the rook on b7 holds the 7th: the king has no
square left.} *

[Event "05. Don't stalemate! (7/8)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "3k4/8/8/1Q6/8/8/8/K3R3 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "05. Don't stalemate! (7/8)"]
[LineDescription "The queen is the piece that stalemates most easily: count the king's squares first."]

{[%csl Bc7,Bc8] [%cal Rb5b7,Rb5c6] Queen and rook again: careful with quiet
queen moves.} 1. Qc5 {Not Qb7 or Qc6: each of them takes both of the king's
squares without check, and it is stalemate! The queen takes the 5th rank: the
wall moves up, and the king is locked in the top 2 rows.} 1... Kd7 {[%csl Bd8]}
2. Re7+ {Check on the 7th rank! The king has to climb to the 8th.} 2... Kd8
{[%cal Ra1a2,Ra1b2,Ra1b1] Careful: Ka2, Kb2 or Kb1 would be stalemate.} 3. Qc7#
{Checkmate! The queen on c7 stands right next to the king, protected by the rook
on e7: the king can neither take it nor run.} *

[Event "05. Don't stalemate! (8/8)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
